  "remaining_integration_work": [
    "Implement the fixed controller event loop and bind the three fixed role runtimes without adding caller callbacks or reopening any public path.",
    "The controller must authenticate READY on the worker-report endpoint before sending ARM to guardian, then retain guardian-armed proof before allowing the worker release sequence to complete.",
    "Bind the broker listener and ledger loop so every offer is durably accepted by the controller and exactly ACKed before the broker can issue CONTINUE; verify worker CONSUMED and terminal aggregate reports.",
    "Transfer each role endpoint through the one-shot v0.117 authority, integrate listener handoff and adoption, worker privilege drop and final seal, guardian-v2 authority consumption, full-size bootstrap and authenticated source closure.",
    "Run a separately authorized bounded Linux native qualification of fork, inherited descriptors, pidfd, waitid, cgroup and channel semantics before any real checkpoint payload read or import, then re-run unchanged admission."
  ],
